@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `il-interpretation-time`

-- Tests for il-interpretation-time.l4.
--
-- Every expected value below was decided from the words of the statute before any module was run
-- (NOTES.md section 0), by hand or with oracle-s10.py, a second reading of s 10 written in Python from the
-- statute's words and not from the L4. A failing assertion is a finding: no expected value here was edited
-- to match what the code computed.
--
-- The days of rest, recess and holiday used below are ILLUSTRATIONS chosen for the tests. They are not a
-- claim about any calendar: the module takes them as an input, and so do these tests.

§ `Tests: counting time`

§§ `Calendars of rest days supplied by the tests`

`no days of rest` MEANS `days of rest, recess or holiday listed in` EMPTY

`rest: Sat 31 Jan 2026` MEANS `days of rest, recess or holiday listed in` (LIST (YMD 2026 1 31))

`rest: Sat 31 Jan and Sun 1 Feb 2026` MEANS `days of rest, recess or holiday listed in` (LIST (YMD 2026 1 31), (YMD 2026 2 1))

`rest: Sat 31 Jan to Mon 2 Feb 2026` MEANS `days of rest, recess or holiday listed in` (LIST (YMD 2026 1 31), (YMD 2026 2 1), (YMD 2026 2 2))

`rest: Fri 30 and Sat 31 Jan 2026` MEANS `days of rest, recess or holiday listed in` (LIST (YMD 2026 1 30), (YMD 2026 1 31))

`rest: Fri 30 Jan to Sun 1 Feb 2026` MEANS `days of rest, recess or holiday listed in` (LIST (YMD 2026 1 30), (YMD 2026 1 31), (YMD 2026 2 1))

`rest: Sat 10 Jan 2026 only` MEANS `days of rest, recess or holiday listed in` (LIST (YMD 2026 1 10))

`rest: Fri 30 Jan 2026 only` MEANS `days of rest, recess or holiday listed in` (LIST (YMD 2026 1 30))

`rest: Sun 1 Feb 2026 only` MEANS `days of rest, recess or holiday listed in` (LIST (YMD 2026 2 1))

`rest: Wed 11 Mar 2026 only` MEANS `days of rest, recess or holiday listed in` (LIST (YMD 2026 3 11))

`rest: Wed 11 and Thu 12 Mar 2026` MEANS `days of rest, recess or holiday listed in` (LIST (YMD 2026 3 11), (YMD 2026 3 12))

`rest: Fri 28 Feb to Sun 2 Mar 2025` MEANS `days of rest, recess or holiday listed in` (LIST (YMD 2025 2 28), (YMD 2025 3 1), (YMD 2025 3 2))

`rest: Sat 28 Feb 2026` MEANS `days of rest, recess or holiday listed in` (LIST (YMD 2026 2 28))

`rest: Thu 15 and Fri 16 Jan 2026` MEANS `days of rest, recess or holiday listed in` (LIST (YMD 2026 1 15), (YMD 2026 1 16))

GIVEN day IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`every day is a rest day` day MEANS TRUE

§§ `s 8 — "until" includes the day it names`

#ASSERT `s 8 — the date` (YMD 2026 3 31) `is up to and including` (YMD 2026 3 31)
#ASSERT `s 8 — the date` (YMD 2026 3 30) `is up to and including` (YMD 2026 3 31)
#ASSERT NOT `s 8 — the date` (YMD 2026 4 1) `is up to and including` (YMD 2026 3 31)
#ASSERT `s 8 — the number` 5 `is up to and including` 5
#ASSERT `s 8 — the number` 4 `is up to and including` 5
#ASSERT NOT `s 8 — the number` 6 `is up to and including` 5
#ASSERT `s 8 — the moment` (`the moment on` (YMD 2026 3 31) `at` 23 `:` 59 `:` 59) `is up to and including` (`the moment on` (YMD 2026 3 31) `at` 23 `:` 59 `:` 59)
#ASSERT NOT `s 8 — the moment` (`the moment on` (YMD 2026 3 31) `at` 23 `:` 59 `:` 59) `is up to and including` (`the moment on` (YMD 2026 3 31) `at` 23 `:` 59 `:` 58)

§§ `s 3 — "day"`

-- A day is the period from midnight until the midnight that follows it.
#ASSERT (`s 3 — the midnight that begins the day` (YMD 2026 3 1))'s `the day` EQUALS YMD 2026 3 1
#ASSERT (`s 3 — the midnight that begins the day` (YMD 2026 3 1))'s `hour` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT (`s 3 — the midnight that ends the day` (YMD 2026 3 1))'s `the day` EQUALS YMD 2026 3 2
#ASSERT (`s 3 — the midnight that ends the day` (YMD 2026 3 31))'s `the day` EQUALS YMD 2026 4 1
#ASSERT (`s 3 — the midnight that ends the day` (YMD 2026 12 31))'s `the day` EQUALS YMD 2027 1 1
#ASSERT (`s 3 — the midnight that ends the day` (YMD 2024 2 28))'s `the day` EQUALS YMD 2024 2 29
#ASSERT (`s 3 — the midnight that ends the day` (YMD 2024 2 29))'s `the day` EQUALS YMD 2024 3 1
#ASSERT (`s 3 — the midnight that ends the day` (YMD 2025 2 28))'s `the day` EQUALS YMD 2025 3 1

-- Twenty-four hours: 86,400 seconds between the two midnights, on an ordinary day and on 29 February.
#ASSERT (`the number of seconds up to` (`s 3 — the midnight that ends the day` (YMD 2026 3 1))) MINUS (`the number of seconds up to` (`s 3 — the midnight that begins the day` (YMD 2026 3 1))) EQUALS 86400
#ASSERT (`the number of seconds up to` (`s 3 — the midnight that ends the day` (YMD 2024 2 29))) MINUS (`the number of seconds up to` (`s 3 — the midnight that begins the day` (YMD 2024 2 29))) EQUALS 86400

-- A moment is within the day: the opening midnight, noon, the last second, and (by s 8's reading of s 3's
-- own "until") the closing midnight; not the second after it, and not the second before the opening midnight.
#ASSERT `s 3 — the moment` (`the moment on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `at` 0 `:` 0 `:` 0) `is within the day` (YMD 2026 3 1)
#ASSERT `s 3 — the moment` (`the moment on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `at` 12 `:` 0 `:` 0) `is within the day` (YMD 2026 3 1)
#ASSERT `s 3 — the moment` (`the moment on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `at` 23 `:` 59 `:` 59) `is within the day` (YMD 2026 3 1)
#ASSERT `s 3 — the moment` (`the moment on` (YMD 2026 3 2) `at` 0 `:` 0 `:` 0) `is within the day` (YMD 2026 3 1)
#ASSERT NOT `s 3 — the moment` (`the moment on` (YMD 2026 3 2) `at` 0 `:` 0 `:` 1) `is within the day` (YMD 2026 3 1)
#ASSERT NOT `s 3 — the moment` (`the moment on` (YMD 2026 2 28) `at` 23 `:` 59 `:` 59) `is within the day` (YMD 2026 3 1)

-- The half-open alternative: the closing midnight is the next day's.
#ASSERT `s 3 — the moment` (`the moment on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `at` 0 `:` 0 `:` 0) `is within the day` (YMD 2026 3 1) `, not counting the closing midnight`
#ASSERT `s 3 — the moment` (`the moment on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `at` 23 `:` 59 `:` 59) `is within the day` (YMD 2026 3 1) `, not counting the closing midnight`
#ASSERT NOT `s 3 — the moment` (`the moment on` (YMD 2026 3 2) `at` 0 `:` 0 `:` 0) `is within the day` (YMD 2026 3 1) `, not counting the closing midnight`

-- The day a moment falls on is the day it is stamped with; the closing midnight of 1 March is the first moment of 2 March.
#ASSERT `s 3 — the day of the moment` (`the moment on` (YMD 2026 3 2) `at` 0 `:` 0 `:` 0) EQUALS YMD 2026 3 2

§§ `s 3 — "year" and "month": which calendar`

#ASSERT `s 3 — the calendar of a year or month specified as` (`Specification of a period of years or months` WITH `beginning by the Hebrew calendar only` IS FALSE, `end by the Hebrew calendar only` IS FALSE) EQUALS `the Gregorian calendar`
#ASSERT `s 3 — the calendar of a year or month specified as` (`Specification of a period of years or months` WITH `beginning by the Hebrew calendar only` IS TRUE, `end by the Hebrew calendar only` IS FALSE) EQUALS `the Hebrew calendar`
#ASSERT `s 3 — the calendar of a year or month specified as` (`Specification of a period of years or months` WITH `beginning by the Hebrew calendar only` IS FALSE, `end by the Hebrew calendar only` IS TRUE) EQUALS `the Hebrew calendar`
#ASSERT `s 3 — the calendar of a year or month specified as` (`Specification of a period of years or months` WITH `beginning by the Hebrew calendar only` IS TRUE, `end by the Hebrew calendar only` IS TRUE) EQUALS `the Hebrew calendar`

-- The Hebrew calendar is not computed: a named refusal, with its exact message.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 3 and s 10(b) — the last day of a period of` 3 `years after an event on` (YMD 2025 7 16) `, counted by` `the Hebrew calendar` BECAUSE "a period counted by the Hebrew calendar needs the Hebrew calendar's months, their lengths and its leap years, which this module does not compute"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 3 and s 10(b) — the last day of a period of` 6 `months after an event on` (YMD 2025 7 16) `, counted by` `the Hebrew calendar` BECAUSE "a period counted by the Hebrew calendar needs the Hebrew calendar's months, their lengths and its leap years, which this module does not compute"
#ASSERT (`s 3 and s 10(b) — the last day of a period of` 3 `years after an event on` (YMD 2025 7 16) `, counted by` `the Gregorian calendar`) EQUALS YMD 2028 7 16
#ASSERT (`s 3 and s 10(b) — the last day of a period of` 6 `months after an event on` (YMD 2025 7 16) `, counted by` `the Gregorian calendar`) EQUALS YMD 2026 1 16

§§ `s 3 — "fiscal year"`

#ASSERT (`s 3 — the first day of the fiscal year` 2026) EQUALS YMD 2026 1 1
#ASSERT (`s 3 — the last day of the fiscal year` 2026) EQUALS YMD 2026 12 31
#ASSERT (`s 3 — the last day of the fiscal year` 2024) EQUALS YMD 2024 12 31
#ASSERT `s 3 — the date` (YMD 2026 1 1) `is in the fiscal year` 2026
#ASSERT `s 3 — the date` (YMD 2026 6 15) `is in the fiscal year` 2026
#ASSERT `s 3 — the date` (YMD 2026 12 31) `is in the fiscal year` 2026
#ASSERT NOT `s 3 — the date` (YMD 2027 1 1) `is in the fiscal year` 2026
#ASSERT NOT `s 3 — the date` (YMD 2025 12 31) `is in the fiscal year` 2026

§§ `s 10(a) — days and weeks from a day: the day itself is not counted`

-- The counted days are D+1 .. D+N, so the last day is D+N.
#ASSERT (`s 10(a) — the last day of a period of` 30 `days from` (YMD 2026 1 1)) EQUALS YMD 2026 1 31
#ASSERT (`s 10(a) — the last day of a period of` 1 `days from` (YMD 2026 3 10)) EQUALS YMD 2026 3 11
#ASSERT (`s 10(a) — the last day of a period of` 1 `weeks from` (YMD 2026 3 10)) EQUALS YMD 2026 3 17
#ASSERT (`s 10(a) — the last day of a period of` 7 `days from` (YMD 2026 3 10)) EQUALS YMD 2026 3 17
#ASSERT (`s 10(a) — the last day of a period of` 2 `weeks from` (YMD 2025 12 25)) EQUALS YMD 2026 1 8
#ASSERT (`s 10(a) — the last day of a period of` 4 `weeks from` (YMD 2026 1 31)) EQUALS YMD 2026 2 28
#ASSERT (`s 10(a) — the last day of a period of` 30 `days from` (YMD 2026 12 15)) EQUALS YMD 2027 1 14
#ASSERT (`s 10(a) — the last day of a period of` 30 `days from` (YMD 2024 2 10)) EQUALS YMD 2024 3 11
#ASSERT (`s 10(a) — the last day of a period of` 365 `days from` (YMD 2024 3 1)) EQUALS YMD 2025 3 1
#ASSERT (`s 10(a) — the last day of a period of` 366 `days from` (YMD 2024 2 28)) EQUALS YMD 2025 2 28
#ASSERT (`s 10(a) — the last day of a period of` 28 `days from` (YMD 2026 2 1)) EQUALS YMD 2026 3 1
#ASSERT (`s 10(a) — the last day of a period of` 28 `days from` (YMD 2024 2 1)) EQUALS YMD 2024 2 29

-- "After" a day, for days and weeks: (a) governs, as it does for "from".
#ASSERT (`s 10 — the last day of a period of` 30 `days after the day` (YMD 2026 1 1)) EQUALS YMD 2026 1 31
#ASSERT (`s 10 — the last day of a period of` 1 `weeks after the day` (YMD 2026 3 10)) EQUALS YMD 2026 3 17

§§ `s 10(b) — months and years after an event: the day with the event's number`

-- The brief's worked cases, from the words of (b).
#ASSERT (`s 10(b) — the last day of a period of` 3 `years after an event on` (YMD 2025 7 16)) EQUALS YMD 2028 7 16
#ASSERT (`s 10(b) — the last day of a period of` 5 `years after an event on` (YMD 2025 1 15)) EQUALS YMD 2030 1 15
#ASSERT (`s 10(b) — the last day of a period of` 5 `years after an event on` (YMD 2025 9 1)) EQUALS YMD 2030 9 1
#ASSERT (`s 10(b) — the last day of a period of` 2 `years after an event on` (YMD 2024 2 28)) EQUALS YMD 2026 2 28
#ASSERT (`s 10(b) — the last day of a period of` 1 `years after an event on` (YMD 2024 2 29)) EQUALS YMD 2025 2 28
#ASSERT (`s 10(b) — the last day of a period of` 1 `months after an event on` (YMD 2025 1 31)) EQUALS YMD 2025 2 28

-- "From" a day, months and years: (b) governs, the day being the day of the event.
#ASSERT (`s 10 — the last day of a period of` 3 `years from the day` (YMD 2025 7 16)) EQUALS YMD 2028 7 16
#ASSERT (`s 10 — the last day of a period of` 5 `years from the day` (YMD 2025 1 15)) EQUALS YMD 2030 1 15
#ASSERT (`s 10 — the last day of a period of` 5 `years from the day` (YMD 2025 9 1)) EQUALS YMD 2030 9 1
#ASSERT (`s 10 — the last day of a period of` 2 `years from the day` (YMD 2024 2 28)) EQUALS YMD 2026 2 28
#ASSERT (`s 10 — the last day of a period of` 1 `years from the day` (YMD 2024 2 29)) EQUALS YMD 2025 2 28
#ASSERT (`s 10 — the last day of a period of` 1 `months from the day` (YMD 2025 1 31)) EQUALS YMD 2025 2 28

-- A start on the 31st, and on other days a short month lacks.
#ASSERT (`s 10(b) — the last day of a period of` 1 `months after an event on` (YMD 2024 1 31)) EQUALS YMD 2024 2 29
#ASSERT (`s 10(b) — the last day of a period of` 1 `months after an event on` (YMD 2025 3 31)) EQUALS YMD 2025 4 30
#ASSERT (`s 10(b) — the last day of a period of` 1 `months after an event on` (YMD 2025 1 30)) EQUALS YMD 2025 2 28
#ASSERT (`s 10(b) — the last day of a period of` 1 `months after an event on` (YMD 2025 1 29)) EQUALS YMD 2025 2 28
#ASSERT (`s 10(b) — the last day of a period of` 1 `months after an event on` (YMD 2024 1 29)) EQUALS YMD 2024 2 29
#ASSERT (`s 10(b) — the last day of a period of` 1 `months after an event on` (YMD 2025 1 28)) EQUALS YMD 2025 2 28
#ASSERT (`s 10(b) — the last day of a period of` 1 `months after an event on` (YMD 2025 5 31)) EQUALS YMD 2025 6 30
#ASSERT (`s 10(b) — the last day of a period of` 2 `months after an event on` (YMD 2025 12 31)) EQUALS YMD 2026 2 28
#ASSERT (`s 10(b) — the last day of a period of` 6 `months after an event on` (YMD 2025 8 31)) EQUALS YMD 2026 2 28
#ASSERT (`s 10(b) — the last day of a period of` 6 `months after an event on` (YMD 2023 8 31)) EQUALS YMD 2024 2 29
#ASSERT (`s 10(b) — the last day of a period of` 3 `months after an event on` (YMD 2025 11 30)) EQUALS YMD 2026 2 28
#ASSERT (`s 10(b) — the last day of a period of` 13 `months after an event on` (YMD 2025 1 31)) EQUALS YMD 2026 2 28
#ASSERT (`s 10(b) — the last day of a period of` 25 `months after an event on` (YMD 2025 1 31)) EQUALS YMD 2027 2 28
#ASSERT (`s 10(b) — the last day of a period of` 1 `months after an event on` (YMD 2025 12 15)) EQUALS YMD 2026 1 15
#ASSERT (`s 10(b) — the last day of a period of` 12 `months after an event on` (YMD 2025 6 15)) EQUALS YMD 2026 6 15

-- A start on 29 February.
#ASSERT (`s 10(b) — the last day of a period of` 1 `months after an event on` (YMD 2024 2 29)) EQUALS YMD 2024 3 29
#ASSERT (`s 10(b) — the last day of a period of` 12 `months after an event on` (YMD 2024 2 29)) EQUALS YMD 2025 2 28
#ASSERT (`s 10(b) — the last day of a period of` 2 `years after an event on` (YMD 2024 2 29)) EQUALS YMD 2026 2 28
#ASSERT (`s 10(b) — the last day of a period of` 3 `years after an event on` (YMD 2024 2 29)) EQUALS YMD 2027 2 28
#ASSERT (`s 10(b) — the last day of a period of` 4 `years after an event on` (YMD 2024 2 29)) EQUALS YMD 2028 2 29
#ASSERT (`s 10(b) — the last day of a period of` 8 `years after an event on` (YMD 2024 2 29)) EQUALS YMD 2032 2 29
#ASSERT (`s 10(b) — the last day of a period of` 76 `years after an event on` (YMD 2024 2 29)) EQUALS YMD 2100 2 28
#ASSERT (`s 10(b) — the last day of a period of` 100 `years after an event on` (YMD 2024 2 29)) EQUALS YMD 2124 2 29
#ASSERT (`s 10(b) — the last day of a period of` 100 `years after an event on` (YMD 2000 2 29)) EQUALS YMD 2100 2 28
#ASSERT (`s 10(b) — the last day of a period of` 400 `years after an event on` (YMD 2000 2 29)) EQUALS YMD 2400 2 29
#ASSERT (`s 10(b) — the last day of a period of` 1 `years after an event on` (YMD 2023 2 28)) EQUALS YMD 2024 2 28
#ASSERT (`s 10(b) — the last day of a period of` 1 `years after an event on` (YMD 2025 6 15)) EQUALS YMD 2026 6 15

-- `daydate`'s `add months` and `add years` were measured on the hard cases: they clamp to the last day of the
-- month, which is what (b) says. The statute governs, and these assertions say where the library agrees with it.
#ASSERT (`add months` (YMD 2025 1 31) 1) EQUALS YMD 2025 2 28
#ASSERT (`add months` (YMD 2024 1 31) 1) EQUALS YMD 2024 2 29
#ASSERT (`add months` (YMD 2025 12 31) 2) EQUALS YMD 2026 2 28
#ASSERT (`add months` (YMD 2025 11 30) 3) EQUALS YMD 2026 2 28
#ASSERT (`add years` (YMD 2024 2 29) 1) EQUALS YMD 2025 2 28
#ASSERT (`add years` (YMD 2024 2 29) 4) EQUALS YMD 2028 2 29
#ASSERT (`add years` (YMD 2024 2 28) 2) EQUALS YMD 2026 2 28

§§ `s 10(c) — a period does not end on a day of rest, recess or holiday`

-- The nominal last day of 30 days from 2026-01-01 is Sat 2026-01-31.
-- No rest days, or a rest day that does not touch the last day: the end does not move.
#ASSERT (`s 10(a), (c) — the last day of a period of` 30 `days from` (YMD 2026 1 1) `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `no days of rest`) EQUALS YMD 2026 1 31
#ASSERT (`s 10(a), (c) — the last day of a period of` 30 `days from` (YMD 2026 1 1) `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `rest: Sat 10 Jan 2026 only`) EQUALS YMD 2026 1 31
#ASSERT (`s 10(a), (c) — the last day of a period of` 30 `days from` (YMD 2026 1 1) `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `rest: Fri 30 Jan 2026 only`) EQUALS YMD 2026 1 31
#ASSERT (`s 10(a), (c) — the last day of a period of` 30 `days from` (YMD 2026 1 1) `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `rest: Sun 1 Feb 2026 only`) EQUALS YMD 2026 1 31

-- One rest day, the last: the period ends on the next day that is not one.
#ASSERT (`s 10(a), (c) — the last day of a period of` 30 `days from` (YMD 2026 1 1) `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `rest: Sat 31 Jan 2026`) EQUALS YMD 2026 2 1

-- Two rest days in a row, the first beyond the nominal end.
#ASSERT (`s 10(a), (c) — the last day of a period of` 30 `days from` (YMD 2026 1 1) `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `rest: Sat 31 Jan and Sun 1 Feb 2026`) EQUALS YMD 2026 2 2

-- Three in a row.
#ASSERT (`s 10(a), (c) — the last day of a period of` 30 `days from` (YMD 2026 1 1) `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `rest: Sat 31 Jan to Mon 2 Feb 2026`) EQUALS YMD 2026 2 3

-- Two rest days in a row that are both INSIDE the nominal period, at its end (the case that tells the readings apart):
-- the end moves to the first day that is not a rest day.
#ASSERT (`s 10(a), (c) — the last day of a period of` 30 `days from` (YMD 2026 1 1) `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `rest: Fri 30 and Sat 31 Jan 2026`) EQUALS YMD 2026 2 1
#ASSERT (`s 10(a), (c) — the last day of a period of` 30 `days from` (YMD 2026 1 1) `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `rest: Fri 30 Jan to Sun 1 Feb 2026`) EQUALS YMD 2026 2 2

-- A period of one day whose only day is a rest day, and a period of two days whose both days are.
#ASSERT (`s 10(a), (c) — the last day of a period of` 1 `days from` (YMD 2026 3 10) `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `rest: Wed 11 Mar 2026 only`) EQUALS YMD 2026 3 12
#ASSERT (`s 10(a), (c) — the last day of a period of` 2 `days from` (YMD 2026 3 10) `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `rest: Wed 11 and Thu 12 Mar 2026`) EQUALS YMD 2026 3 13
#ASSERT (`s 10(a), (c) — the last day of a period of` 1 `days from` (YMD 2026 3 10) `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `no days of rest`) EQUALS YMD 2026 3 11

-- A rest day in the MIDDLE of the period is counted, so it never moves the end: 28 days from 2026-01-01 ends on 2026-01-29.
#ASSERT (`s 10(a), (c) — the last day of a period of` 28 `days from` (YMD 2026 1 1) `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `rest: Sat 10 Jan 2026 only`) EQUALS YMD 2026 1 29

-- Weeks.
#ASSERT (`s 10(a), (c) — the last day of a period of` 2 `weeks from` (YMD 2026 1 1) `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `rest: Thu 15 and Fri 16 Jan 2026`) EQUALS YMD 2026 1 17
#ASSERT (`s 10(a), (c) — the last day of a period of` 2 `weeks from` (YMD 2026 1 1) `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `no days of rest`) EQUALS YMD 2026 1 15

-- (c) applied to months and years (the reading taken). Without it, the nominal day stands.
#ASSERT (`s 10(b) — the last day of a period of` 1 `months after an event on` (YMD 2025 1 31)) EQUALS YMD 2025 2 28
#ASSERT (`s 10(b), (c) — the last day of a period of` 1 `months after an event on` (YMD 2025 1 31) `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `rest: Fri 28 Feb to Sun 2 Mar 2025`) EQUALS YMD 2025 3 3
#ASSERT (`s 10(b), (c) — the last day of a period of` 1 `months after an event on` (YMD 2025 1 31) `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `no days of rest`) EQUALS YMD 2025 2 28
#ASSERT (`s 10(b), (c) — the last day of a period of` 2 `years after an event on` (YMD 2024 2 28) `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `rest: Sat 28 Feb 2026`) EQUALS YMD 2026 3 1
#ASSERT (`s 10(b), (c) — the last day of a period of` 2 `years after an event on` (YMD 2024 2 28) `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `no days of rest`) EQUALS YMD 2026 2 28

-- (c) on its own, with a calendar given as a function rather than a list.
#ASSERT (`s 10(c) — the last day of a period whose nominal last day is` (YMD 2026 1 31) `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` (GIVEN d YIELD d EQUALS YMD 2026 1 31)) EQUALS YMD 2026 2 1
#ASSERT (`s 10(c) — the last day of a period whose nominal last day is` (YMD 2026 1 30) `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` (GIVEN d YIELD d EQUALS YMD 2026 1 31)) EQUALS YMD 2026 1 30

§§ `Whether a date falls inside a period: the last day in, the next day out`

-- 30 days from 2026-01-01, no rest days: 2026-01-01 is the event day, outside; 01-02 .. 01-31 inside.
#ASSERT NOT `s 10 — the date` (YMD 2026 1 1) `is inside a period of` 30 `days from` (YMD 2026 1 1) `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `no days of rest`
#ASSERT `s 10 — the date` (YMD 2026 1 2) `is inside a period of` 30 `days from` (YMD 2026 1 1) `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `no days of rest`
#ASSERT `s 10 — the date` (YMD 2026 1 31) `is inside a period of` 30 `days from` (YMD 2026 1 1) `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `no days of rest`
#ASSERT NOT `s 10 — the date` (YMD 2026 2 1) `is inside a period of` 30 `days from` (YMD 2026 1 1) `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `no days of rest`
#ASSERT NOT `s 10 — the date` (YMD 2025 12 31) `is inside a period of` 30 `days from` (YMD 2026 1 1) `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `no days of rest`

-- The same with 2026-01-31 a rest day: the period runs to 2026-02-01.
#ASSERT `s 10 — the date` (YMD 2026 1 31) `is inside a period of` 30 `days from` (YMD 2026 1 1) `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `rest: Sat 31 Jan 2026`
#ASSERT `s 10 — the date` (YMD 2026 2 1) `is inside a period of` 30 `days from` (YMD 2026 1 1) `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `rest: Sat 31 Jan 2026`
#ASSERT NOT `s 10 — the date` (YMD 2026 2 2) `is inside a period of` 30 `days from` (YMD 2026 1 1) `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `rest: Sat 31 Jan 2026`

-- One week from 2026-03-10.
#ASSERT NOT `s 10 — the date` (YMD 2026 3 10) `is inside a period of` 1 `weeks from` (YMD 2026 3 10) `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `no days of rest`
#ASSERT `s 10 — the date` (YMD 2026 3 11) `is inside a period of` 1 `weeks from` (YMD 2026 3 10) `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `no days of rest`
#ASSERT `s 10 — the date` (YMD 2026 3 17) `is inside a period of` 1 `weeks from` (YMD 2026 3 10) `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `no days of rest`
#ASSERT NOT `s 10 — the date` (YMD 2026 3 18) `is inside a period of` 1 `weeks from` (YMD 2026 3 10) `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `no days of rest`

-- One month after 2025-01-31.
#ASSERT NOT `s 10 — the date` (YMD 2025 1 31) `is inside a period of` 1 `months after an event on` (YMD 2025 1 31) `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `no days of rest`
#ASSERT `s 10 — the date` (YMD 2025 2 1) `is inside a period of` 1 `months after an event on` (YMD 2025 1 31) `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `no days of rest`
#ASSERT `s 10 — the date` (YMD 2025 2 28) `is inside a period of` 1 `months after an event on` (YMD 2025 1 31) `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `no days of rest`
#ASSERT NOT `s 10 — the date` (YMD 2025 3 1) `is inside a period of` 1 `months after an event on` (YMD 2025 1 31) `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `no days of rest`

-- Three years after 2025-07-16.
#ASSERT NOT `s 10 — the date` (YMD 2025 7 16) `is inside a period of` 3 `years after an event on` (YMD 2025 7 16) `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `no days of rest`
#ASSERT `s 10 — the date` (YMD 2025 7 17) `is inside a period of` 3 `years after an event on` (YMD 2025 7 16) `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `no days of rest`
#ASSERT `s 10 — the date` (YMD 2028 7 16) `is inside a period of` 3 `years after an event on` (YMD 2025 7 16) `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `no days of rest`
#ASSERT NOT `s 10 — the date` (YMD 2028 7 17) `is inside a period of` 3 `years after an event on` (YMD 2025 7 16) `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `no days of rest`

-- One year after 2024-02-29: ends on 2025-02-28.
#ASSERT NOT `s 10 — the date` (YMD 2024 2 29) `is inside a period of` 1 `years after an event on` (YMD 2024 2 29) `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `no days of rest`
#ASSERT `s 10 — the date` (YMD 2024 3 1) `is inside a period of` 1 `years after an event on` (YMD 2024 2 29) `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `no days of rest`
