-- Two years after 2024-02-28, ending on Sat 2026-02-28 which is made a rest day: the period runs to 2026-03-01.
#ASSERT `s 10 — the date` (YMD 2026 2 28) `is inside a period of` 2 `years after an event on` (YMD 2024 2 28) `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `rest: Sat 28 Feb 2026`
#ASSERT `s 10 — the date` (YMD 2026 3 1) `is inside a period of` 2 `years after an event on` (YMD 2024 2 28) `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `rest: Sat 28 Feb 2026`
#ASSERT NOT `s 10 — the date` (YMD 2026 3 2) `is inside a period of` 2 `years after an event on` (YMD 2024 2 28) `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `rest: Sat 28 Feb 2026`

§§ `Where the module gives no answer`

-- A period fixed in a number of days, weeks, months or years has a positive whole number of them.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 10(a) — the last day of a period of` 0 `days from` (YMD 2026 1 1) BECAUSE "s 10 speaks of a period fixed in a number of days, weeks, months or years; the number given is not a positive whole number"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 10(a) — the last day of a period of` (0 MINUS 5) `days from` (YMD 2026 1 1) BECAUSE "s 10 speaks of a period fixed in a number of days, weeks, months or years; the number given is not a positive whole number"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 10(a) — the last day of a period of` 2.5 `days from` (YMD 2026 1 1) BECAUSE "s 10 speaks of a period fixed in a number of days, weeks, months or years; the number given is not a positive whole number"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 10(a) — the last day of a period of` 0 `weeks from` (YMD 2026 1 1) BECAUSE "s 10 speaks of a period fixed in a number of days, weeks, months or years; the number given is not a positive whole number"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 10(b) — the last day of a period of` 0 `months after an event on` (YMD 2026 1 1) BECAUSE "s 10 speaks of a period fixed in a number of days, weeks, months or years; the number given is not a positive whole number"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 10(b) — the last day of a period of` 1.5 `years after an event on` (YMD 2026 1 1) BECAUSE "s 10 speaks of a period fixed in a number of days, weeks, months or years; the number given is not a positive whole number"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 10(b), (c) — the last day of a period of` 0 `years after an event on` (YMD 2026 1 1) `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `no days of rest` BECAUSE "s 10 speaks of a period fixed in a number of days, weeks, months or years; the number given is not a positive whole number"

-- A calendar of rest days with no ordinary day within a year: the walk of (c) is bounded at 366 days, and says so.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 10(c) — the last day of a period whose nominal last day is` (YMD 2026 1 31) `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `every day is a rest day` BECAUSE "s 10(c) gives no answer if the supplied calendar of rest days has no day that is not a rest day within a year"

§§ `s 21 — the moment a statute begins to bind`

-- A statute commencing on 2026-03-01 begins to bind at 00:01 on that day.
#ASSERT (`s 21 — the moment a statute begins to bind, commencing on` (YMD 2026 3 1))'s `the day` EQUALS YMD 2026 3 1
#ASSERT (`s 21 — the moment a statute begins to bind, commencing on` (YMD 2026 3 1))'s `hour` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT (`s 21 — the moment a statute begins to bind, commencing on` (YMD 2026 3 1))'s `minute` EQUALS 1
#ASSERT (`s 21 — the moment a statute begins to bind, commencing on` (YMD 2026 3 1))'s `second` EQUALS 0

-- Binds from 00:01:00; not at 00:00:00, not at 00:00:59; not on the day before; and from then on.
#ASSERT `s 21 — the moment` (`the moment on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `at` 0 `:` 1 `:` 0) `is one at which a statute commencing on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `binds`
#ASSERT `s 21 — the moment` (`the moment on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `at` 0 `:` 1 `:` 1) `is one at which a statute commencing on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `binds`
#ASSERT `s 21 — the moment` (`the moment on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `at` 12 `:` 0 `:` 0) `is one at which a statute commencing on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `binds`
#ASSERT `s 21 — the moment` (`the moment on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `at` 23 `:` 59 `:` 59) `is one at which a statute commencing on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `binds`
#ASSERT `s 21 — the moment` (`the moment on` (YMD 2026 3 2) `at` 0 `:` 0 `:` 0) `is one at which a statute commencing on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `binds`
#ASSERT NOT `s 21 — the moment` (`the moment on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `at` 0 `:` 0 `:` 0) `is one at which a statute commencing on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `binds`
#ASSERT NOT `s 21 — the moment` (`the moment on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `at` 0 `:` 0 `:` 59) `is one at which a statute commencing on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `binds`
#ASSERT NOT `s 21 — the moment` (`the moment on` (YMD 2026 2 28) `at` 23 `:` 59 `:` 59) `is one at which a statute commencing on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `binds`
#ASSERT NOT `s 21 — the moment` (`the moment on` (YMD 2025 3 1) `at` 12 `:` 0 `:` 0) `is one at which a statute commencing on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `binds`

-- A statute that fixes a moment of its own displaces the default; one that fixes none gets 00:01.
#ASSERT (`s 21 — the moment a statute commencing on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `begins to bind, unless it fixes a moment of its own:` NOTHING)'s `minute` EQUALS 1
#ASSERT (`s 21 — the moment a statute commencing on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `begins to bind, unless it fixes a moment of its own:` (JUST (`the moment on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `at` 12 `:` 0 `:` 0)))'s `hour` EQUALS 12
#ASSERT (`s 21 — the moment a statute commencing on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `begins to bind, unless it fixes a moment of its own:` (JUST (`the moment on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `at` 12 `:` 0 `:` 0)))'s `minute` EQUALS 0

§§ `Interpretation Ordinance s 17 — when regulations of legislative effect come into force`

-- Published on 2026-05-14, with no other provision: in force on that day.
#ASSERT (`Ordinance s 17 — the day regulations of legislative effect come into force, published on` (YMD 2026 5 14) `unless another provision fixes the day:` NOTHING) EQUALS YMD 2026 5 14

-- Another provision fixes a later day: that day, not the day of publication.
#ASSERT (`Ordinance s 17 — the day regulations of legislative effect come into force, published on` (YMD 2026 5 14) `unless another provision fixes the day:` (JUST (YMD 2026 6 1))) EQUALS YMD 2026 6 1

-- Read with Law s 21: they bind from 00:01 on that day.
#ASSERT (`Ordinance s 17, Law s 21 — the moment regulations of legislative effect begin to bind, published on` (YMD 2026 5 14) `unless another provision fixes the day:` NOTHING)'s `the day` EQUALS YMD 2026 5 14
#ASSERT (`Ordinance s 17, Law s 21 — the moment regulations of legislative effect begin to bind, published on` (YMD 2026 5 14) `unless another provision fixes the day:` NOTHING)'s `minute` EQUALS 1
#ASSERT (`Ordinance s 17, Law s 21 — the moment regulations of legislative effect begin to bind, published on` (YMD 2026 5 14) `unless another provision fixes the day:` (JUST (YMD 2026 6 1)))'s `the day` EQUALS YMD 2026 6 1
